      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143472",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},\u2026,{X}_{16}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}\u223cPo(\\theta )$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{16},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{16}{x}_{i}=18,\\,{\\prod }_{i=1}^{16}({x}_{i})!=6.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a Poisson distribution is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\theta }^{x}{e}^{-\\theta }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,\u2026\n$$"
